2. Gmarket Sans
   Copyright (c) 2019 eBay Korea Co., Ltd., with Reserved Font Name "Gmarket Sans Font".
   SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/LICENSES/GmarketSans-OFL.txt).
   Bundled as assets/fonts/GmarketSans-{Light,Medium,Bold}.woff2.

   This is the Gmarket Sans distribution licence as embedded in the original fonts
   (name ID 13). Besides the five standard OFL conditions it has a sixth: images of work
   produced with the font (printouts, advertising, online video) may be used by the
   copyright holder to promote the font unless the user explicitly declines.

   The .woff2 files are WOFF2 encodings of the original TrueType files made with
   fontTools (woff2.compress, no recalculation). Decoded and compared with the originals,
   the glyph outlines and instructions of all 12,262 glyphs, the name table and every
   other table are unchanged, except for what the WOFF2 encoding itself does: glyf/loca
   are stored in the WOFF2 transformed form, head.flags bit 11 is set and the checksum
   recomputed, and the original 8-byte DSIG table — an empty stub with zero signatures —
   is dropped because WOFF2 encoding invalidates signatures. No WOFF metadata was added.
   On that basis the original names are kept (OFL FAQ 2.2.1). Subsetting or otherwise
   editing these files creates a Modified Version, which must not use the Reserved Font
   Name.

3. Hansung University signature
   assets/brand/hsu-signature-en{,-white,-blue}.svg are the HSU UI English horizontal
   signature, converted from Hansung University's official .ai file with
   scripts/brand_ai2svg.py (outlines unchanged, page cropped to the artwork, colours
   kept or set to one colour). The signature is a Hansung University mark; it is
   included to build materials for Hansung University and VILAB.

Hansung University brand color values are institutional brand specifications and are
used here to build interfaces for Hansung University and VILAB.

The design tokens (assets/tokens.css, fonts.css, base.css) are copied from
hs-vilab-frontend-design by the same author. They contain no third-party text.

scripts/scan_slop.py is copied unchanged (a provenance note added at the top) from
